  "question": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0143_fa46475a9dfa.jpg\" style=\"width: 132px; height: 164px;\" /><br /><br />Given in the figure are two blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, respectively. These are being pressed against a wall by a force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> and kept in equilibrium as shown. If the coefficient of friction between the blocks is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and between block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and the wall is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></math>, the frictional force applied by the wall on block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
